Subject: [PATCH] Molten Core: Majordomo Flamewaker Healers are the first target, Elites after

WHY THIS PATCH EXISTS

Majordomo Executus brings 8 adds, 4 Flamewaker Healers (11663) and 4
Flamewaker Elites (11664), and the encounter ends when all 8 are dead. The
moltencore strategy only keeps damage off Majordomo himself, so the bots split
their damage over healers and elites alike, and the healers keep the elites
alive. This is patch 3 of 4 for the encounter and builds on patches 0017 and
0018, which edit the same function.

WHAT IT DOES

For damage target selection, the Flamewaker Elites are excluded in the same
hook that already excludes Majordomo, the reflecting adds and the shielded
adds, while a Flamewaker Healer is alive and within reach of this bot. Reach
means: in the bot's attackers list (alive and not immune), not excluded for
this bot by the Magic Reflection or Damage Shield branches, within spell
distance, and in line of sight. The exclusion is recomputed on every call, so
it ends the moment the last reachable healer dies, goes out of reach or is
excluded: the bot is never left without a target because of a healer it
cannot hit. This repo's tests pin the single condition for "a healer is in
reach".

WHAT THIS PATCH DELIBERATELY DOES NOT DO

It does not touch the reflect hold (patch 0017), the Damage Shield step-off
(patch 0018) or the threat after Teleport Target (patch 4). It uses the DPS
target exclusion only, so tanks keep their own target selection. It keys on
the two add entries by id, so no other encounter is affected. It is an
exclusion, not a priority: the fork exposes no priority hook, so the first
target is whichever healer the fork's own selection picks.

WHEN THIS PATCH SHOULD BE DELETED

When the fork's Molten Core strategy orders the Majordomo adds itself.

diff --git a/src/Ai/Raid/MC/MCStrategy.cpp b/src/Ai/Raid/MC/MCStrategy.cpp
index 1a31df1..f7604b3 100644
--- a/src/Ai/Raid/MC/MCStrategy.cpp
+++ b/src/Ai/Raid/MC/MCStrategy.cpp
@@ -148,6 +148,37 @@ void RaidMcStrategy::AppendTargetExclusions(GuidSet& exclusions, TargetValueExcl
             exclusions.insert(guid);
     }
 
+    // Kill order: the Flamewaker Healers die first, the Elites after. While a
+    // healer is alive, this bot can see it, and it is not itself excluded
+    // above, the Elites are left alone. A healer that is excluded, out of
+    // spell range, out of line of sight, dead or immune does not count (the
+    // attackers list holds only valid targets), so the Elites are open to
+    // the bot again and it never waits on a healer it cannot reach.
+    bool const healersFirst = type == TargetValueExclusionType::DpsTarget;
+    bool healerInReach = false;
+    if (healersFirst)
+    {
+        for (ObjectGuid const guid : AI_VALUE(GuidVector, "attackers"))
+        {
+            Unit* unit = botAI->GetUnit(guid);
+            if (unit && unit->GetEntry() == NPC_FLAMEWAKER_HEALER && exclusions.find(guid) == exclusions.end() &&
+                bot->GetDistance(unit) <= sPlayerbotAIConfig.SpellDistance && bot->IsWithinLOSInMap(unit))
+            {
+                healerInReach = true;
+                break;
+            }
+        }
+    }
+    if (healerInReach)
+    {
+        for (ObjectGuid const guid : AI_VALUE(GuidVector, "attackers"))
+        {
+            Unit* unit = botAI->GetUnit(guid);
+            if (unit && unit->GetEntry() == NPC_FLAMEWAKER_ELITE)
+                exclusions.insert(guid);
+        }
+    }
+
     if (reflecting)
     {
